   "id": "h2-6",
   "name": "Micronutrients and their deficiencies"
  }
 ],
 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Micronutrients are vitamins and minerals, needed in very small amounts but essential for health.\nHidden hunger is a lack of micronutrients: a person may eat enough food (and not feel hungry) but still lack vitamins and minerals. It is common where meals are mostly starchy staples (cassava, maize, rice) with few vegetables, fruits or animal foods.\nCommon deficiencies:\n• iron: anaemia (tiredness, pale eyelids and palms);\n• iodine: goitre (a swollen neck) and poor mental development;\n• vitamin A: night blindness, infections;\n• vitamin C: scurvy (bleeding gums);\n• vitamin D or calcium: rickets (soft, bent bones).\nPrevention: a varied diet with fruits, vegetables and animal foods; iodised salt; fortified foods.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "n": "Bih"
  },
  "problem": "{n} eats garri and fufu every day, rarely vegetables, fruit or meat. She feels tired and her eyelids are pale. What may be wrong, and what should she eat?",
  "steps": [
   "Her meals are mostly starch: she may have hidden hunger.",
   "Tiredness and pale eyelids are signs of anaemia, a lack of iron.",
   "She should add iron-rich foods: green leaves (huckleberry, njama njama), beans, liver, meat, fish."
  ],
  "answer": "Probably anaemia (lack of iron); eat green leaves, beans, liver, meat or fish.",
  "checks": []
 },
